<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Random Colour Picker | Choose a Colour</title><meta name="description" content="Pick a random colour from a custom list or use the built-in starter palette. Useful for crafts, classroom groups, games and creative prompts."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/colour-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a><a href="/picture-picker">Picture Picker</a><a href="/student-picker">Student Picker</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Creative tool</span><h1>Random Colour Picker</h1><p>Choose from named colours you enter yourself. The selected colour is shown as both text and a swatch, making the tool useful for art prompts, team labels and playful choices.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="grid"><div class="field"><label for="colours">Colour names</label><textarea id="colours">Red
Orange
Yellow
Green
Blue
Purple
Pink
Teal</textarea></div><div class="field"><label for="mode">After picking</label><select id="mode"><option value="keep">Keep colours in the list</option><option value="remove">Remove selected colour</option></select><div class="actions"><button id="pick">Pick a colour</button><button class="secondary" id="reset">Restore palette</button></div></div></div><div class="result" id="result"><div class="big-choice">Ready</div></div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>A colour picker that uses your own list</h2><p>This page chooses from the colour names you provide rather than generating an arbitrary hexadecimal value. That makes it easier to use with real supplies, classroom resources or game pieces. If you only have red, blue, green and yellow markers, those can be the entire pool.</p></section><section><h2>Creative uses</h2><ul><li>Choose the main colour for a drawing, collage or craft challenge.</li><li>Assign colour-coded classroom groups when colours already have a meaning in the room.</li><li>Pick a paint, marker or pencil family before starting a quick creative exercise.</li><li>Choose a colour theme for a digital design warm-up.</li><li>Add chance to scavenger hunts by selecting the colour of the next object to find.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Named colours and screen colours are different things</h2><p>The swatch uses the browser's interpretation of common colour names. If you type a name the browser does not recognise, the text result will still be selected but the visual swatch may fall back to a neutral colour. Physical paints, pencils and fabrics can also look very different from a screen.</p></section><section><h2>Remove mode for no-repeat rounds</h2><p>Use remove-after-pick mode when every colour should appear once before any repeat. This works well for multi-round creative prompts. Keep mode is better when each round should start with the full set of options again.</p></section><section><h2>Related creative tools</h2><div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/picture-picker">Picture Picker<span>Randomly choose from images on your device.</span></a><a class="card" href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker<span>Choose from custom activity prompts.</span></a><a class="card" href="/random-number-picker">Number Picker<span>Add numeric constraints to a creative exercise.</span></a></div></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),sample='Red\nOrange\nYellow\nGreen\nBlue\nPurple\nPink\nTeal';function list(){return $('colours').value.split(/\n|,/).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean)}$('pick').onclick=()=>{const a=list();if(!a.length)return $('result').innerHTML='<div class="big-choice">Add a colour</div>';const i=Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length),v=a[i];const probe=document.createElement('span');probe.style.color='';probe.style.color=v;const valid=probe.style.color!=='';$('result').innerHTML=`<div style="height:120px;border-radius:14px;background:${valid?v:'#2a2840'};border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15)"></div><div class="big-choice">${v}</div>`;if($('mode').value==='remove'){a.splice(i,1);$('colours').value=a.join('\n')}};$('reset').onclick=()=>{$('colours').value=sample;$('result').innerHTML='<div class="big-choice">Ready</div>'};</script></body></html>